window._jstEnglishData = [{"book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"And God sent an angel unto Jerusalem to destroy it. And the angel stretched forth his hand unto Jerusalem to destroy it; and God said to the angel, Stay now thine hand, it is enough; for as he was destroying, the Lord beheld Israel, that he repented him of the evil; therefore the Lord stayed the angel that destroyed, as he stood by the threshing floor of Ornan, the Jebusite."},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Now concerning the things whereof ye wrote unto me, saying, It is good for a man not to touch a woman."},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"Nevertheless, I say, to avoid fornication, let every man have his own wife, and let every woman have her own husband."},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":1,"verse":3,"english":"Depart ye not one from the other, except it be with consent for a time, that ye may give yourselves to fasting and prayer; and come together again, that Satan tempt you not for your incontinency."},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":1,"verse":4,"english":"I suppose therefore that this is good for the present distress, for a man so to remain that he may do greater good."},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":1,"verse":5,"english":"So then he that giveth himself in marriage doeth well; but he that giveth himself not in marriage doeth better."},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"Also celestial bodies, and bodies terrestrial, and bodies telestial; but the glory of the celestial, one; and the terrestrial, another; and the telestial, another."},{"book":"1 John","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"My little children, these things write I unto you, that ye sin not. But if any man sin and repent, we have an advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ the righteous;"},{"book":"1 John","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"Whosoever is born of God doth not continue in sin; for the Spirit of God remaineth in him; and he cannot continue in sin, because he is born of God, having received that holy Spirit of promise."},{"book":"1 John","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"No man hath seen God at any time, except them who believe. If we love one another, God dwelleth in us, and his love is perfected in us."},{"book":"1 Peter","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Some of whom were disobedient in the days of Noah, while the long-suffering of God waited, while the ark was preparing, wherein few, that is, eight souls were saved by water."},{"book":"1 Peter","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"Because of this, is the gospel preached to them who are dead, that they might be judged according to men in the flesh, but live in the spirit according to the will of God."},{"book":"1 Peter","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"And above all things have fervent charity among yourselves; for charity preventeth a multitude of sins."},{"book":"1 Samuel","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"But the Spirit of the Lord departed from Saul, and an evil spirit which was not of the Lord troubled him."},{"book":"1 Samuel","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"And Saul’s servants said unto him, Behold now, an evil spirit which is not of God troubleth thee."},{"book":"1 Samuel","chapter":1,"verse":3,"english":"Let our lord now command thy servants, which are before thee, to seek out a man, who is a cunning player on a harp; and it shall come to pass, when the evil spirit, which is not of God, is upon thee, that he shall play with his hand, and thou shalt be well."},{"book":"1 Samuel","chapter":1,"verse":4,"english":"And it came to pass, when the evil spirit, which was not of God, was upon Saul, that David took a harp, and played with his hand; so Saul was refreshed, and was well, and the evil spirit departed from him."},{"book":"1 Thessalonians","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"For this we say unto you by the word of the Lord, that they who are alive at the coming of the Lord, shall not prevent them who remain unto the coming of the Lord, who are asleep."},{"book":"1 Timothy","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Who is willing to have all men to be saved, and to come unto the knowledge of the truth which is in Christ Jesus, who is the Only Begotten Son of God, and ordained to be a Mediator between God and man; who is one God, and hath power over all men."},{"book":"1 Timothy","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"But if I tarry long, that thou mayest know how thou oughtest to behave thyself in the house of God, which is the church of the living God."},{"book":"1 Timothy","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"The pillar and ground of the truth is, (and without controversy, great is the mystery of godliness,) God was manifest in the flesh, justified in the Spirit, seen of angels, preached unto the Gentiles, believed on in the world, received up into glory."},{"book":"1 Timothy","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"Which in his times he shall show, who is the blessed and only Potentate, the King of kings, and Lord of lords, to whom be honor and power everlasting;"},{"book":"1 Timothy","chapter":3,"verse":2,"english":"Whom no man hath seen, nor can see, unto whom no man can approach, only he who hath the light and the hope of immortality dwelling in him."},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Now therefore, behold, the Lord hath found a lying spirit in the mouth of these thy prophets, and the Lord hath spoken evil against thee."},{"book":"2 Corinthians","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Wherefore, henceforth live we no more after the flesh; yea, though we once lived after the flesh, yet since we have known Christ, now henceforth live we no more after the flesh."},{"book":"2 Peter","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Knowing this first, that in the last days there shall come scoffers, walking after their own lusts."},{"book":"2 Peter","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"Denying the Lord Jesus Christ, and saying, Where is the promise of his coming? for since the fathers fell asleep, all things must continue as they are, and have continued as they are from the beginning of the creation."},{"book":"2 Peter","chapter":1,"verse":3,"english":"For this they willingly are ignorant of, that of old the heavens, and the earth standing in the water and out of the water, were created by the word of God;"},{"book":"2 Peter","chapter":1,"verse":4,"english":"And by the word of God, the world that then was, being overflowed with water perished;"},{"book":"2 Peter","chapter":1,"verse":5,"english":"But the heavens, and the earth which are now, are kept in store by the same word, reserved unto fire against the day of judgment and perdition of ungodly men."},{"book":"2 Peter","chapter":1,"verse":6,"english":"Nevertheless, if we shall endure, we shall be kept according to his promise. And we look for a new heavens, and a new earth wherein dwelleth righteousness."},{"book":"2 Samuel","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"And David said unto Nathan, I have sinned against the Lord. And Nathan said unto David, The Lord also hath not put away thy sin that thou shalt not die."},{"book":"2 Thessalonians","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"That ye be not soon shaken in mind, or be troubled by letter, except ye receive it from us; neither by spirit, nor by word, as that the day of Christ is at hand."},{"book":"2 Thessalonians","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"Let no man deceive you by any means; for there shall come a falling away first, and that man of sin be revealed, the son of perdition;"},{"book":"2 Thessalonians","chapter":1,"verse":3,"english":"For the mystery of iniquity doth already work, and he it is who now worketh, and Christ suffereth him to work, until the time is fulfilled that he shall be taken out of the way."},{"book":"2 Thessalonians","chapter":1,"verse":4,"english":"And then shall that wicked one be revealed, whom the Lord shall consume with the spirit of his mouth, and shall destroy with the brightness of his coming."},{"book":"2 Thessalonians","chapter":1,"verse":5,"english":"Yea, the Lord, even Jesus, whose coming is not until after there cometh a falling away, by the working of Satan with all power, and signs and lying wonders,"},{"book":"Acts","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"And they who were journeying with him saw indeed the light, and were afraid; but they heard not the voice of him who spake to him."},{"book":"Acts","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"Then straightway they departed from him which should have examined him, and the chief captain also was afraid after he knew that he was a Roman, because he had bound him, and he loosed him from his bands."},{"book":"Acts","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"On the morrow, because he would have known the certainty wherefore he was accused of the Jews, he commanded the chief priests and all their council to appear, and brought Paul down, and set him before them."},{"book":"Amos","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"And the Lord said, concerning Jacob, Jacob shall repent for this, therefore I will not utterly destroy him, saith the Lord."},{"book":"Colossians","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Which are after the doctrines and commandments of men, who teach you to touch not, taste not, handle not; all those things which are to perish with the using?"},{"book":"Colossians","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"Which things have indeed a show of wisdom in will worship, and humility, and neglecting the body as to the satisfying the flesh, not in any honor to God."},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"And I will write on the tables the words that were on the first tables, which thou brakest, save the words of the everlasting covenant of the holy priesthood, and thou shalt put them in the ark."},{"book":"Ephesians","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Can ye be angry, and not sin? let not the sun go down upon your wrath;"},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"And the Lord said unto Moses, When thou goest to return into Egypt, see that thou do all those wonders before Pharaoh, which I have put in thine hand, and I will prosper thee; but Pharaoh will harden his heart, and he will not let the people go."},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"And it came to pass, that the Lord appeared unto him as he was in the way, by the inn. The Lord was angry with Moses, and his hand was about to fall upon him, to kill him; for he had not circumcised his son."},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":1,"verse":3,"english":"Then Zipporah took a sharp stone and circumcised her son, and cast the stone at his feet, and said, Surely thou art a bloody husband unto me."},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":1,"verse":4,"english":"And the Lord spared Moses and let him go, because Zipporah, his wife, circumcised the child. And she said, Thou art a bloody husband. And Moses was ashamed, and hid his face from the Lord, and said, I have sinned before the Lord."},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":1,"verse":5,"english":"And the Lord said unto Aaron, Go into the wilderness to meet Moses, and he went and met him, in the mount of God; in the mount where God appeared unto him; and Aaron kissed him."},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"When Jethro, the high priest of Midian, Moses’ father-in-law, heard of all that God had done for Moses, and for Israel his people, and that the Lord had brought Israel out of Egypt;"},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"Thou shalt not suffer a murderer to live."},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":4,"verse":1,"english":"And the Lord said unto Moses, If they will repent of the evil which they have done, I will spare them, and turn away my fierce wrath; but, behold, thou shalt execute judgment upon all that will not repent of this evil this day. Therefore, see thou do this thing that I have commanded thee, or I will execute all that which I had thought to do unto my people."},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":5,"verse":1,"english":"And he said unto Moses, Thou canst not see my face at this time, lest mine anger be kindled against thee also, and I destroy thee, and thy people; for there shall no man among them see me at this time, and live, for they are exceeding sinful. And no sinful man hath at any time, neither shall there be any sinful man at any time, that shall see my face and live."},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":5,"verse":2,"english":"And I will take away mine hand, and thou shalt see my back parts, but my face shall not be seen, as at other times; for I am angry with my people Israel."},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":6,"verse":1,"english":"And the Lord said unto Moses, Hew thee two other tables of stone, like unto the first, and I will write upon them also, the words of the law, according as they were written at the first on the tables which thou brakest; but it shall not be according to the first, for I will take away the priesthood out of their midst; therefore my holy order, and the ordinances thereof, shall not go before them; for my presence shall not go up in their midst, lest I destroy them."},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":6,"verse":2,"english":"But I will give unto them the law as at the first, but it shall be after the law of a carnal commandment; for I have sworn in my wrath, that they shall not enter into my presence, into my rest, in the days of their pilgrimage. Therefore do as I have commanded thee, and be ready in the morning, and come up in the morning unto mount Sinai, and present thyself there to me, in the top of the mount."},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":6,"verse":3,"english":"For thou shalt worship no other god; for the Lord, whose name is Jehovah, is a jealous God."},{"book":"Galatians","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Wherefore then, the law was added because of transgressions, till the seed should come to whom the promise was made in the law given to Moses, who was ordained by the hand of angels to be a mediator of this first covenant, (the law.)"},{"book":"Galatians","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"Now this mediator was not a mediator of the new covenant; but there is one mediator of the new covenant, who is Christ, as it is written in the law concerning the promises made to Abraham and his seed. Now Christ is the mediator of life; for this is the promise which God made unto Abraham."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"JST, Genesis 1–8. The Joseph Smith Translation of Genesis 1–8 is published in the Pearl of Great Price as the book of Moses. See the book of Moses."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"And Noah builded an altar unto the Lord, and took of every clean beast, and of every clean fowl, and offered burnt offerings on the altar; and gave thanks unto the Lord, and rejoiced in his heart."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"And the Lord spake unto Noah, and he blessed him. And Noah smelled a sweet savor, and he said in his heart;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":3,"english":"I will call on the name of the Lord, that he will not again curse the ground any more for man’s sake, for the imagination of man’s heart is evil from his youth; and that he will not again smite any more every thing living, as he hath done, while the earth remaineth;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":4,"english":"But, the blood of all flesh which I have given you for meat, shall be shed upon the ground, which taketh life thereof, and the blood ye shall not eat."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":5,"english":"And surely, blood shall not be shed, only for meat, to save your lives; and the blood of every beast will I require at your hands."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":6,"english":"And whoso sheddeth man’s blood, by man shall his blood be shed; for man shall not shed the blood of man."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":7,"english":"For a commandment I give, that every man’s brother shall preserve the life of man, for in mine own image have I made man."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":8,"english":"And a commandment I give unto you, Be ye fruitful and multiply; bring forth abundantly on the earth, and multiply therein."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":9,"english":"And God spake unto Noah, and to his sons with him, saying, And I, behold, I will establish my covenant with you, which I made unto your father Enoch, concerning your seed after you."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":10,"english":"And the bow shall be in the cloud; and I will look upon it, that I may remember the everlasting covenant, which I made unto thy father Enoch; that, when men should keep all my commandments, Zion should again come on the earth, the city of Enoch which I have caught up unto myself."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":11,"english":"And this is mine everlasting covenant, that when thy posterity shall embrace the truth, and look upward, then shall Zion look downward, and all the heavens shall shake with gladness, and the earth shall tremble with joy;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":12,"english":"And the general assembly of the church of the firstborn shall come down out of heaven, and possess the earth, and shall have place until the end come. And this is mine everlasting covenant, which I made with thy father Enoch."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":13,"english":"And the bow shall be in the cloud, and I will establish my covenant unto thee, which I have made between me and thee, for every living creature of all flesh that shall be upon the earth."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"verse":14,"english":"And God said unto Noah, This is the token of the covenant which I have established between me and thee; for all flesh that shall be upon the earth."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"And Melchizedek lifted up his voice and blessed Abram."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":2,"english":"Now Melchizedek was a man of faith, who wrought righteousness; and when a child he feared God, and stopped the mouths of lions, and quenched the violence of fire."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":3,"english":"And thus, having been approved of God, he was ordained an high priest after the order of the covenant which God made with Enoch,"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":4,"english":"It being after the order of the Son of God; which order came, not by man, nor the will of man; neither by father nor mother; neither by beginning of days nor end of years; but of God;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":5,"english":"And it was delivered unto men by the calling of his own voice, according to his own will, unto as many as believed on his name."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":6,"english":"For God having sworn unto Enoch and unto his seed with an oath by himself; that every one being ordained after this order and calling should have power, by faith, to break mountains, to divide the seas, to dry up waters, to turn them out of their course;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":7,"english":"To put at defiance the armies of nations, to divide the earth, to break every band, to stand in the presence of God; to do all things according to his will, according to his command, subdue principalities and powers; and this by the will of the Son of God which was from before the foundation of the world."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":8,"english":"And men having this faith, coming up unto this order of God, were translated and taken up into heaven."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":9,"english":"And now, Melchizedek was a priest of this order; therefore he obtained peace in Salem, and was called the Prince of peace."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":10,"english":"And his people wrought righteousness, and obtained heaven, and sought for the city of Enoch which God had before taken, separating it from the earth, having reserved it unto the latter days, or the end of the world;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":11,"english":"And hath said, and sworn with an oath, that the heavens and the earth should come together; and the sons of God should be tried so as by fire."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":12,"english":"And this Melchizedek, having thus established righteousness, was called the king of heaven by his people, or, in other words, the King of peace."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":13,"english":"And he lifted up his voice, and he blessed Abram, being the high priest, and the keeper of the storehouse of God;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":14,"english":"Him whom God had appointed to receive tithes for the poor."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":15,"english":"Wherefore, Abram paid unto him tithes of all that he had, of all the riches which he possessed, which God had given him more than that which he had need."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"verse":16,"english":"And it came to pass, that God blessed Abram, and gave unto him riches, and honor, and lands for an everlasting possession; according to the covenant which he had made, and according to the blessing wherewith Melchizedek had blessed him."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":4,"verse":1,"english":"And Abram said, Lord God, how wilt thou give me this land for an everlasting inheritance?"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":4,"verse":2,"english":"And the Lord said, Though thou wast dead, yet am I not able to give it thee?"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":4,"verse":3,"english":"And if thou shalt die, yet thou shalt possess it, for the day cometh, that the Son of Man shall live; but how can he live if he be not dead? he must first be quickened."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":4,"verse":4,"english":"And it came to pass, that Abram looked forth and saw the days of the Son of Man, and was glad, and his soul found rest, and he believed in the Lord; and the Lord counted it unto him for righteousness."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":1,"english":"And it came to pass, that Abram fell on his face, and called upon the name of the Lord."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":2,"english":"And God talked with him, saying, My people have gone astray from my precepts, and have not kept mine ordinances, which I gave unto their fathers;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":3,"english":"And they have not observed mine anointing, and the burial, or baptism wherewith I commanded them;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":4,"english":"But have turned from the commandment, and taken unto themselves the washing of children, and the blood of sprinkling;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":5,"english":"And have said that the blood of the righteous Abel was shed for sins; and have not known wherein they are accountable before me."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":6,"english":"But as for thee, behold, I will make my covenant with thee, and thou shalt be a father of many nations."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":7,"english":"And this covenant I make, that thy children may be known among all nations. Neither shall thy name any more be called Abram, but thy name shall be called Abraham; for, a father of many nations have I made thee."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":8,"english":"And I will make thee exceedingly fruitful, and I will make nations of thee, and kings shall come of thee, and of thy seed."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":9,"english":"And I will establish a covenant of circumcision with thee, and it shall be my covenant between me and thee, and thy seed after thee, in their generations; that thou mayest know forever that children are not accountable before me until they are eight years old."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":10,"english":"And thou shalt observe to keep all my covenants wherein I covenanted with thy fathers; and thou shalt keep the commandments which I have given thee with mine own mouth, and I will be a God unto thee and thy seed after thee."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":11,"english":"Then Abraham fell on his face and rejoiced, and said in his heart, There shall a child be born unto him that is an hundred years old, and Sarah that is ninety years old shall bear."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":5,"verse":12,"english":"And Abraham said unto God, Oh that Ishmael might live uprightly before thee!"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":6,"verse":1,"english":"And they said unto him, Stand back. And they were angry with him."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":6,"verse":2,"english":"And they said among themselves, This one man came in to sojourn among us, and he will needs now make himself to be a judge; now we will deal worse with him than with them."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":6,"verse":3,"english":"Wherefore they said unto the man, We will have the men, and thy daughters also; and we will do with them as seemeth us good."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":6,"verse":4,"english":"Now this was after the wickedness of Sodom."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":6,"verse":5,"english":"And Lot said, Behold now, I have two daughters which have not known man; let me, I pray you, plead with my brethren that I may not bring them out unto you; and ye shall not do unto them as seemeth good in your eyes;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":6,"verse":6,"english":"For God will not justify his servant in this thing; wherefore, let me plead with my brethren, this once only, that unto these men ye do nothing, that they may have peace in my house; for therefore came they under the shadow of my roof."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":6,"verse":7,"english":"And they were angry with Lot and came near to break the door, but the angels of God, which were holy men, put forth their hand and pulled Lot into the house unto them, and shut the door."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":7,"verse":1,"english":"Then Abimelech, and Phicol, the chief captain of his hosts, rose up, and they planted a grove in Beer-sheba, and called there on the name of the Lord; and they returned unto the land of the Philistines."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":7,"verse":2,"english":"And Abraham worshiped the everlasting God, and sojourned in the land of the Philistines many days."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":8,"verse":1,"english":"And now, of thy two sons, Ephraim and Manasseh, which were born unto thee in the land of Egypt, before I came unto thee into Egypt; behold, they are mine, and the God of my fathers shall bless them; even as Reuben and Simeon they shall be blessed, for they are mine; wherefore they shall be called after my name. (Therefore they were called Israel.)"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":8,"verse":2,"english":"And thy issue which thou begettest after them, shall be thine, and shall be called after the name of their brethren in their inheritance, in the tribes; therefore they were called the tribes of Manasseh and of Ephraim."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":8,"verse":3,"english":"And Jacob said unto Joseph, When the God of my fathers appeared unto me in Luz, in the land of Canaan; he sware unto me, that he would give unto me, and unto my seed, the land for an everlasting possession."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":8,"verse":4,"english":"Therefore, O my son, he hath blessed me in raising thee up to be a servant unto me, in saving my house from death;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":8,"verse":5,"english":"In delivering my people, thy brethren, from famine which was sore in the land; wherefore the God of thy fathers shall bless thee, and the fruit of thy loins, that they shall be blessed above thy brethren, and above thy father’s house;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":8,"verse":6,"english":"For thou hast prevailed, and thy father’s house hath bowed down unto thee, even as it was shown unto thee, before thou wast sold into Egypt by the hands of thy brethren; wherefore thy brethren shall bow down unto thee, from generation to generation, unto the fruit of thy loins forever;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":8,"verse":7,"english":"For thou shalt be a light unto my people, to deliver them in the days of their captivity, from bondage; and to bring salvation unto them, when they are altogether bowed down under sin."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":1,"english":"And Joseph said unto his brethren, I die, and go unto my fathers; and I go down to my grave with joy. The God of my father Jacob be with you, to deliver you out of affliction in the days of your bondage; for the Lord hath visited me, and I have obtained a promise of the Lord, that out of the fruit of my loins, the Lord God will raise up a righteous branch out of my loins; and unto thee, whom my father Jacob hath named Israel, a prophet; (not the Messiah who is called Shilo;) and this prophet shall deliver my people out of Egypt in the days of thy bondage."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":2,"english":"And it shall come to pass that they shall be scattered again; and a branch shall be broken off, and shall be carried into a far country; nevertheless they shall be remembered in the covenants of the Lord, when the Messiah cometh; for he shall be made manifest unto them in the latter days, in the Spirit of power; and shall bring them out of darkness into light; out of hidden darkness, and out of captivity unto freedom."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":3,"english":"A seer shall the Lord my God raise up, who shall be a choice seer unto the fruit of my loins."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":4,"english":"Thus saith the Lord God of my fathers unto me, A choice seer will I raise up out of the fruit of thy loins, and he shall be esteemed highly among the fruit of thy loins; and unto him will I give commandment that he shall do a work for the fruit of thy loins, his brethren."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":5,"english":"And he shall bring them to the knowledge of the covenants which I have made with thy fathers; and he shall do whatsoever work I shall command him."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":6,"english":"And I will make him great in mine eyes, for he shall do my work; and he shall be great like unto him whom I have said I would raise up unto you, to deliver my people, O house of Israel, out of the land of Egypt; for a seer will I raise up to deliver my people out of the land of Egypt; and he shall be called Moses. And by this name he shall know that he is of thy house; for he shall be nursed by the king’s daughter, and shall be called her son."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":7,"english":"And again, a seer will I raise up out of the fruit of thy loins, and unto him will I give power to bring forth my word unto the seed of thy loins; and not to the bringing forth of my word only, saith the Lord, but to the convincing them of my word, which shall have already gone forth among them in the last days;"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":8,"english":"Wherefore the fruit of thy loins shall write, and the fruit of the loins of Judah shall write; and that which shall be written by the fruit of thy loins, and also that which shall be written by the fruit of the loins of Judah, shall grow together unto the confounding of false doctrines, and laying down of contentions, and establishing peace among the fruit of thy loins, and bringing them to a knowledge of their fathers in the latter days; and also to the knowledge of my covenants, saith the Lord."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":9,"english":"And out of weakness shall he be made strong, in that day when my work shall go forth among all my people, which shall restore them, who are of the house of Israel, in the last days."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":10,"english":"And that seer will I bless, and they that seek to destroy him shall be confounded; for this promise I give unto you; for I will remember you from generation to generation; and his name shall be called Joseph, and it shall be after the name of his father; and he shall be like unto you; for the thing which the Lord shall bring forth by his hand shall bring my people unto salvation."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":11,"english":"And the Lord sware unto Joseph that he would preserve his seed forever, saying, I will raise up Moses, and a rod shall be in his hand, and he shall gather together my people, and he shall lead them as a flock, and he shall smite the waters of the Red Sea with his rod."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":12,"english":"And he shall have judgment, and shall write the word of the Lord. And he shall not speak many words, for I will write unto him my law by the finger of mine own hand. And I will make a spokesman for him, and his name shall be called Aaron."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":13,"english":"And it shall be done unto thee in the last days also, even as I have sworn. Therefore, Joseph said unto his brethren, God will surely visit you, and bring you out of this land, unto the land which he sware unto Abraham, and unto Isaac, and to Jacob."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":14,"english":"And Joseph confirmed many other things unto his brethren, and took an oath of the children of Israel, saying unto them, God will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence."},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verse":15,"english":"So Joseph died when he was an hundred and ten years old; and they embalmed him, and they put him in a coffin in Egypt; and he was kept from burial by the children of Israel, that he might be carried up and laid in the sepulchre with his father. And thus they remembered the oath which they sware unto him."},{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"And again, when he bringeth in the first begotten into the world, he saith, And let all the angels of God worship him, who maketh his ministers as a flame of fire."},{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"And of the angels he saith, Angels are ministering spirits."},{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"For we who have believed do enter into rest, as he said, As I have sworn in my wrath, If they harden their hearts they shall not enter into my rest; also, I have sworn, If they will not harden their hearts, they shall enter into my rest; although the works of God were prepared, (or finished,) from the foundation of the world."},{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"Therefore not leaving the principles of the doctrine of Christ, let us go on unto perfection; not laying again the foundation of repentance from dead works, and of faith toward God."},{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":3,"verse":2,"english":"Of the doctrine of baptisms, of laying on of hands, and of the resurrection of the dead, and of eternal judgment."},{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":3,"verse":3,"english":"And we will go on unto perfection if God permit."},{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":4,"verse":1,"english":"For this Melchizedek was ordained a priest after the order of the Son of God, which order was without father, without mother, without descent, having neither beginning of days, nor end of life. And all those who are ordained unto this priesthood are made like unto the Son of God, abiding a priest continually."},{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":4,"verse":2,"english":"For the law was administered without an oath and made nothing perfect, but was only the bringing in of a better hope; by the which we draw nigh unto God."},{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":4,"verse":3,"english":"Inasmuch as this high priest was not without an oath, by so much was Jesus made the surety of a better testament."},{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":5,"verse":1,"english":"Now faith is the assurance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen."},{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":5,"verse":2,"english":"Women received their dead raised to life again; and others were tortured, not accepting deliverance; that they might obtain the first resurrection;"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Woe to Ariel, to Ariel, the city where David dwelt! add ye year to year; let them kill sacrifices."},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"Yet I will distress Ariel, and there shall be heaviness and sorrow; for thus hath the Lord said unto me, It shall be unto Ariel;"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":1,"verse":3,"english":"That I the Lord will camp against her round about, and will lay siege against her with a mount, and I will raise forts against her."},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":1,"verse":4,"english":"And she shall be brought down, and shall speak out of the ground, and her speech shall be low out of the dust; and her voice shall be as of one that hath a familiar spirit, out of the ground, and her speech shall whisper out of the dust."},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":1,"verse":5,"english":"Moreover the multitude of her strangers shall be like small dust, and the multitude of the terrible ones shall be as chaff that passeth away; yea, it shall be at an instant suddenly."},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":1,"verse":6,"english":"For they shall be visited of the Lord of hosts with thunder, and with earthquake, and great noise, with storm and tempest, and the flame of devouring fire."},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":1,"verse":7,"english":"And the multitude of all the nations that fight against Ariel, even all that fight against her and her munition, and that distress her, shall be as a dream of a night vision."},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":1,"verse":8,"english":"Yea, it shall be unto them even as unto a hungry man who dreameth, and behold, he eateth, but he awaketh and his soul is empty; or like unto a thirsty man who dreameth, and behold, he drinketh, but he awaketh, and behold, he is faint, and his soul hath appetite. Yea, even so shall the multitude of all the nations be that fight against mount Zion."},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"For I will send my servant unto you who are blind; yea, a messenger to open the eyes of the blind, and unstop the ears of the deaf;"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"And they shall be made perfect notwithstanding their blindness, if they will hearken unto the messenger, the Lord’s servant."},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":2,"verse":3,"english":"Thou art a people, seeing many things, but thou observest not; opening the ears to hear, but thou hearest not."},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":2,"verse":4,"english":"The Lord is not well pleased with such a people, but for his righteousness’ sake he will magnify the law and make it honorable."},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":2,"verse":5,"english":"Thou art a people robbed and spoiled; thine enemies, all of them, have snared thee in holes, and they have hid thee in prison houses; they have taken thee for a prey, and none delivereth; for a spoil, and none saith, Restore."},{"book":"James","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into many afflictions;"},{"book":"James","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"My brethren, ye cannot have the faith of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Lord of glory, and yet have respect to persons."},{"book":"James","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"What profit is it, my brethren, for a man to say he hath faith, and hath not works? can faith save him?"},{"book":"James","chapter":2,"verse":3,"english":"Yea, a man may say, I will show thee I have faith without works; but I say, Show me thy faith without works, and I will show thee my faith by my works."},{"book":"James","chapter":2,"verse":4,"english":"Even so faith, if it have not works is dead, being alone."},{"book":"James","chapter":2,"verse":5,"english":"Therefore wilt thou know, O vain man, that faith without works is dead and cannot save you?"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Therefore now, amend your ways and your doings, and obey the voice of the Lord your God, and repent, and the Lord will turn away the evil that he hath pronounced against you."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"In the beginning was the gospel preached through the Son. And the gospel was the word, and the word was with the Son, and the Son was with God, and the Son was of God."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"The same was in the beginning with God."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":3,"english":"All things were made by him; and without him was not anything made which was made."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":4,"english":"In him was the gospel, and the gospel was the life, and the life was the light of men;"},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":5,"english":"And the light shineth in the world, and the world perceiveth it not."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":6,"english":"There was a man sent from God, whose name was John."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":7,"english":"The same came into the world for a witness, to bear witness of the light, to bear record of the gospel through the Son, unto all, that through him men might believe."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":8,"english":"He was not that light, but came to bear witness of that light,"},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":9,"english":"Which was the true light, which lighteth every man who cometh into the world;"},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":10,"english":"Even the Son of God. He who was in the world, and the world was made by him, and the world knew him not."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":11,"english":"He came unto his own, and his own received him not."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":12,"english":"But as many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God; only to them who believe on his name."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":13,"english":"He was born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":14,"english":"And the same word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the Only Begotten of the Father, full of grace and truth."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":15,"english":"John bear witness of him, and cried, saying, This is he of whom I spake; He who cometh after me, is preferred before me; for he was before me."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":16,"english":"For in the beginning was the Word, even the Son, who is made flesh, and sent unto us by the will of the Father. And as many as believe on his name shall receive of his fullness. And of his fullness have all we received, even immortality and eternal life, through his grace."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":17,"english":"For the law was given through Moses, but life and truth came through Jesus Christ."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":18,"english":"For the law was after a carnal commandment, to the administration of death; but the gospel was after the power of an endless life, through Jesus Christ, the Only Begotten Son, who is in the bosom of the Father."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":19,"english":"And no man hath seen God at any time, except he hath borne record of the Son; for except it is through him no man can be saved."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":20,"english":"And this is the record of John, when the Jews sent priests and Levites from Jerusalem, to ask him; Who art thou?"},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":21,"english":"And he confessed, and denied not that he was Elias; but confessed, saying; I am not the Christ."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":22,"english":"And they asked him, saying; How then art thou Elias? And he said, I am not that Elias who was to restore all things. And they asked him, saying, Art thou that prophet? And he answered, No."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":23,"english":"Then said they unto him, Who art thou? that we may give an answer to them that sent us. What sayest thou of thyself?"},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":24,"english":"He said, I am the voice of one crying in the wilderness, Make straight the way of the Lord, as saith the prophet Esaias."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":25,"english":"And they who were sent were of the Pharisees."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":26,"english":"And they asked him, and said unto him; Why baptizest thou then, if thou be not the Christ, nor Elias who was to restore all things, neither that prophet?"},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":27,"english":"John answered them, saying; I baptize with water, but there standeth one among you, whom ye know not;"},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":28,"english":"He it is of whom I bear record. He is that prophet, even Elias, who, coming after me, is preferred before me, whose shoe’s latchet I am not worthy to unloose, or whose place I am not able to fill; for he shall baptize, not only with water, but with fire, and with the Holy Ghost."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":29,"english":"The next day John seeth Jesus coming unto him, and said; Behold the Lamb of God, who taketh away the sin of the world!"},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":30,"english":"And John bare record of him unto the people, saying, This is he of whom I said; After me cometh a man who is preferred before me; for he was before me, and I knew him, and that he should be made manifest to Israel; therefore am I come baptizing with water."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":31,"english":"And John bare record, saying; When he was baptized of me, I saw the Spirit descending from heaven like a dove, and it abode upon him."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":32,"english":"And I knew him; for he who sent me to baptize with water, the same said unto me; Upon whom thou shalt see the Spirit descending, and remaining on him, the same is he who baptizeth with the Holy Ghost."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":33,"english":"And I saw, and bare record that this is the Son of God."},{"book":"John","chapter":1,"verse":34,"english":"These things were done in Bethabara, beyond Jordan, where John was baptizing."},{"book":"John","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"When therefore the Pharisees had heard that Jesus made and baptized more disciples than John,"},{"book":"John","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"They sought more diligently some means that they might put him to death; for many received John as a prophet, but they believed not on Jesus."},{"book":"John","chapter":2,"verse":3,"english":"Now the Lord knew this, though he himself baptized not so many as his disciples;"},{"book":"John","chapter":2,"verse":4,"english":"For he suffered them for an example, preferring one another."},{"book":"John","chapter":2,"verse":5,"english":"For unto such hath God promised his Spirit. And they who worship him, must worship in spirit and in truth."},{"book":"John","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"No man can come unto me, except he doeth the will of my Father who hath sent me. And this is the will of him who hath sent me, that ye receive the Son; for the Father beareth record of him; and he who receiveth the testimony, and doeth the will of him who sent me, I will raise up in the resurrection of the just."},{"book":"John","chapter":4,"verse":1,"english":"Peter saith unto him, Thou needest not to wash my feet. Jesus answered him, If I wash thee not, thou hast no part with me."},{"book":"John","chapter":4,"verse":2,"english":"Simon Peter saith unto him, Lord, not my feet only, but also my hands and my head."},{"book":"John","chapter":4,"verse":3,"english":"Jesus saith to him, He that has washed his hands and his head, needeth not save to wash his feet, but is clean every whit; and ye are clean, but not all. Now this was the custom of the Jews under their law; wherefore, Jesus did this that the law might be fulfilled."},{"book":"John","chapter":5,"verse":1,"english":"Hereafter I will not talk much with you; for the prince of darkness, who is of this world, cometh, but hath no power over me, but he hath power over you."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"And while he executed the priest’s office before God, in the order of his priesthood,"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"And it came to pass, after three days they found him in the temple, sitting in the midst of the doctors, and they were hearing him, and asking him questions."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"As it is written in the book of the prophet Esaias; and these are the words, saying, The voice of one crying in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord, and make his paths straight."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":3,"verse":2,"english":"For behold, and lo, he shall come, as it is written in the book of the prophets, to take away the sins of the world, and to bring salvation unto the heathen nations, to gather together those who are lost, who are of the sheepfold of Israel;"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":3,"verse":3,"english":"Yea, even the dispersed and afflicted; and also to prepare the way, and make possible the preaching of the gospel unto the Gentiles;"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":3,"verse":4,"english":"And to be a light unto all who sit in darkness, unto the uttermost parts of the earth; to bring to pass the resurrection from the dead, and to ascend up on high, to dwell on the right hand of the Father,"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":3,"verse":5,"english":"Until the fullness of time, and the law and the testimony shall be sealed, and the keys of the kingdom shall be delivered up again unto the Father;"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":3,"verse":6,"english":"To administer justice unto all; to come down in judgment upon all, and to convince all the ungodly of their ungodly deeds, which they have committed; and all this in the day that he shall come;"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":3,"verse":7,"english":"For it is a day of power; yea, every valley shall be filled, and every mountain and hill shall be brought low; the crooked shall be made straight, and the rough ways made smooth;"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":3,"verse":8,"english":"And all flesh shall see the salvation of God."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":4,"verse":1,"english":"And unto him who smiteth thee on the cheek, offer also the other; or, in other words, it is better to offer the other, than to revile again. And him who taketh away thy cloak, forbid not to take thy coat also."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":4,"verse":2,"english":"For it is better that thou suffer thine enemy to take these things, than to contend with him. Verily I say unto you, Your heavenly Father who seeth in secret, shall bring that wicked one into judgment."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":5,"verse":1,"english":"For whosoever will save his life, must be willing to lose it for my sake; and whosoever will be willing to lose his life for my sake, the same shall save it."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":5,"verse":2,"english":"For what doth it profit a man if he gain the whole world, and yet he receive him not whom God hath ordained, and he lose his own soul, and he himself be a castaway?"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":6,"verse":1,"english":"Woe unto you, lawyers! For ye have taken away the key of knowledge, the fullness of the scriptures; ye enter not in yourselves into the kingdom; and those who were entering in, ye hindered."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":7,"verse":1,"english":"But he who denieth me before men, shall be denied before the angels of God."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":7,"verse":2,"english":"Now his disciples knew that he said this, because they had spoken evil against him before the people; for they were afraid to confess him before men."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":7,"verse":3,"english":"And they reasoned among themselves, saying, He knoweth our hearts, and he speaketh to our condemnation, and we shall not be forgiven. But he answered them, and said unto them,"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":7,"verse":4,"english":"Whosoever shall speak a word against the Son of man, and repenteth, it shall be forgiven him; but unto him who blasphemeth against the Holy Ghost, it shall not be forgiven him."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":7,"verse":5,"english":"For, behold, he cometh in the first watch of the night, and he shall also come in the second watch, and again he shall come in the third watch."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":8,"verse":1,"english":"Then certain of them came to him, saying, Good Master, we have Moses and the prophets, and whosoever shall live by them, shall he not have life?"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":8,"verse":2,"english":"And Jesus answered, saying, Ye know not Moses, neither the prophets; for if ye had known them, ye would have believed on me; for to this intent they were written. For I am sent that ye might have life. Therefore I will liken it unto salt which is good;"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":8,"verse":3,"english":"But if the salt has lost its savor, wherewith shall it be seasoned?"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":9,"verse":1,"english":"And they said unto him, We have the law, and the prophets; but as for this man we will not receive him to be our ruler; for he maketh himself to be a judge over us."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":9,"verse":2,"english":"Then said Jesus unto them, The law and the prophets testify of me; yea, and all the prophets who have written, even until John, have foretold of these days."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":9,"verse":3,"english":"Since that time, the kingdom of God is preached, and every man who seeketh truth presseth into it."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":9,"verse":4,"english":"And it is easier for heaven and earth to pass, than for one tittle of the law to fail."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":9,"verse":5,"english":"And why teach ye the law, and deny that which is written; and condemn him whom the Father hath sent to fulfill the law, that ye might all be redeemed?"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":9,"verse":6,"english":"O fools! for you have said in your hearts, There is no God. And you pervert the right way; and the kingdom of heaven suffereth violence of you; and you persecute the meek; and in your violence you seek to destroy the kingdom; and ye take the children of the kingdom by force. Woe unto you, ye adulterers!"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":10,"verse":1,"english":"Neither shall they say, Lo, here! or, Lo, there! For, behold, the kingdom of God has already come unto you."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":10,"verse":2,"english":"And they answered and said unto him, Where, Lord, shall they be taken?"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":10,"verse":3,"english":"And he said unto them, Wheresoever the body is gathered; or, in other words, whithersoever the saints are gathered, thither will the eagles be gathered together; or, thither will the remainder be gathered together."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":10,"verse":4,"english":"This he spake, signifying the gathering of his saints; and of angels descending and gathering the remainder unto them; the one from the bed, the other from the grinding, and the other from the field, whithersoever he listeth."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":10,"verse":5,"english":"For verily there shall be new heavens, and a new earth, wherein dwelleth righteousness."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":10,"verse":6,"english":"And there shall be no unclean thing; for the earth becoming old, even as a garment, having waxed in corruption, wherefore it vanisheth away, and the footstool remaineth sanctified, cleansed from all sin."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":11,"verse":1,"english":"And he said unto them, It is impossible for them who trust in riches, to enter into the kingdom of God; but he who forsaketh the things which are of this world, it is possible with God, that he should enter in."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":12,"verse":1,"english":"Now these things he spake unto them, concerning the destruction of Jerusalem. And then his disciples asked him, saying, Master, tell us concerning thy coming?"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":12,"verse":2,"english":"And he answered them, and said, In the generation in which the times of the Gentiles shall be fulfilled, there shall be signs in the sun, and in the moon, and in the stars; and upon the earth distress of nations with perplexity, like the sea and the waves roaring. The earth also shall be troubled, and the waters of the great deep;"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":12,"verse":3,"english":"Men’s hearts failing them for fear, and for looking after those things which are coming on the earth. For the powers of heaven shall be shaken."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":12,"verse":4,"english":"Verily I say unto you, this generation, the generation when the times of the Gentiles be fulfilled, shall not pass away till all be fulfilled."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":13,"verse":1,"english":"Then said Jesus, Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do (Meaning the soldiers who crucified him,) and they parted his raiment and cast lots."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":14,"verse":1,"english":"And they found the stone rolled away from the sepulcher, and two angels standing by it in shining garments."},{"book":"Luke","chapter":14,"verse":2,"english":"And they entered into the sepulcher, and not finding the body of the Lord Jesus, they were much perplexed thereabout;"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":14,"verse":3,"english":"And were affrighted, and bowed down their faces to the earth. But behold the angels said unto them, Why seek ye the living among the dead?"},{"book":"Mark","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"Wherefore the Sabbath was given unto man for a day of rest; and also that man should glorify God, and not that man should not eat;"},{"book":"Mark","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"For the Son of man made the Sabbath day, therefore the Son of man is Lord also of the Sabbath."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"And then came certain men unto him, accusing him, saying, Why do ye receive sinners, seeing thou makest thyself the Son of God."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"But he answered them and said, Verily I say unto you, All sins which men have committed, when they repent, shall be forgiven them; for I came to preach repentance unto the sons of men."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":2,"verse":3,"english":"And blasphemies, wherewith soever they shall blaspheme, shall be forgiven them that come unto me, and do the works which they see me do."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":2,"verse":4,"english":"But there is a sin which shall not be forgiven. He that shall blaspheme against the Holy Ghost, hath never forgiveness; but is in danger of being cut down out of the world. And they shall inherit eternal damnation."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":2,"verse":5,"english":"And this he said unto them because they said, He hath an unclean spirit."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"Full well is it written of you, by the prophets whom ye have rejected."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":3,"verse":2,"english":"They testified these things of a truth, and their blood shall be upon you."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":3,"verse":3,"english":"Ye have kept not the ordinances of God; for Moses said, Honor thy father and thy mother; and whoso curseth father or mother, let him die the death of the transgressor, as it is written in your law; but ye keep not the law."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":4,"verse":1,"english":"For whosoever will save his life, shall lose it; or whosoever will save his life, shall be willing to lay it down for my sake; and if he is not willing to lay it down for my sake, he shall lose it."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":4,"verse":2,"english":"But whosoever shall be willing to lose his life for my sake, and the gospel, the same shall save it."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":4,"verse":3,"english":"And they shall not have part in that resurrection when he cometh."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":4,"verse":4,"english":"For verily I say unto you, That he shall come; and he that layeth down his life for my sake and the gospel’s, shall come with him, and shall be clothed with his glory in the cloud, on the right hand of the Son of man."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":5,"verse":1,"english":"And there appeared unto them Elias with Moses, or in other words, John the Baptist and Moses; and they were talking with Jesus."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":5,"verse":2,"english":"Therefore, if thy hand offend thee, cut it off; or if thy brother offend thee and confess not and forsake not, he shall be cut off. It is better for thee to enter into life maimed, than having two hands, to go into hell."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":5,"verse":3,"english":"For it is better for thee to enter into life without thy brother, than for thee and thy brother to be cast into hell; into the fire that never shall be quenched, where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":5,"verse":4,"english":"And again, if thy foot offend thee, cut it off; for he that is thy standard, by whom thou walkest, if he become a transgressor, he shall be cut off."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":6,"verse":1,"english":"He is not therefore the God of the dead, but the God of the living; for he raiseth them up out of their graves. Ye therefore do greatly err."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":7,"verse":1,"english":"And as they did eat, Jesus took bread and blessed it, and brake, and gave to them, and said, Take it, and eat."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":7,"verse":2,"english":"Behold, this is for you to do in remembrance of my body; for as oft as ye do this ye will remember this hour that I was with you."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":7,"verse":3,"english":"And he took the cup, and when he had given thanks, he gave it to them; and they all drank of it."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":7,"verse":4,"english":"And he said unto them, This is in remembrance of my blood which is shed for many, and the new testament which I give unto you; for of me ye shall bear record unto all the world."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":7,"verse":5,"english":"And as oft as ye do this ordinance, ye will remember me in this hour that I was with you and drank with you of this cup, even the last time in my ministry."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":7,"verse":6,"english":"Verily I say unto you, Of this ye shall bear record; for I will no more drink of the fruit of the vine with you, until that day that I drink it new in the kingdom of God."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":7,"verse":7,"english":"And now they were grieved, and wept over him."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":8,"verse":1,"english":"But when they looked, they saw that the stone was rolled away, (for it was very great,) and two angels sitting thereon, clothed in long white garments; and they were affrighted."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":8,"verse":2,"english":"But the angels said unto them, Be not affrighted; ye seek Jesus of Nazareth, who was crucified; he is risen; he is not here; behold the place where they laid him;"},{"book":"Mark","chapter":8,"verse":3,"english":"And go your way, tell his disciples and Peter, that he goeth before you into Galilee; there shall ye see him as he said unto you."},{"book":"Mark","chapter":8,"verse":4,"english":"And they, entering into the sepulcher, saw the place where they laid Jesus."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"And when he had gathered all the chief priests, and scribes of the people together, he demanded of them, saying, Where is the place that is written of by the prophets, in which Christ should be born? For he greatly feared, yet he believed not the prophets."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"And they said unto him, It is written by the prophets, that he should be born in Bethlehem of Judea, for thus have they said,"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":1,"verse":3,"english":"The word of the Lord came unto us, saying, And thou Bethlehem, which lieth in the land of Judea, in thee shall be born a prince, which art not the least among the princes of Judea; for out of thee shall come the Messiah, who shall save my people Israel."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":1,"verse":4,"english":"And it came to pass that Jesus grew up with his brethren, and waxed strong, and waited upon the Lord for the time of his ministry to come."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":1,"verse":5,"english":"And he served under his father, and he spake not as other men, neither could he be taught; for he needed not that any man should teach him."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":1,"verse":6,"english":"And after many years, the hour of his ministry drew nigh."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"Then Jesus was led up of the Spirit, into the wilderness, to be with God."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"Then Jesus was taken up into the holy city, and the Spirit setteth him on the pinnacle of the temple."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":2,"verse":3,"english":"Then the devil came unto him and said, If thou be the Son of God, cast thyself down, for it is written, He shall give his angels charge concerning thee, and in their hands they shall bear thee up, lest at any time thou dash thy foot against a stone."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":2,"verse":4,"english":"And again, Jesus was in the Spirit, and it taketh him up into an exceeding high mountain, and showeth him all the kingdoms of the world and the glory of them."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":2,"verse":5,"english":"And the devil came unto him again, and said, All these things will I give unto thee, if thou wilt fall down and worship me."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":2,"verse":6,"english":"And now Jesus knew that John was cast into prison, and he sent angels, and, behold, they came and ministered unto him."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"Whosoever, therefore, shall break one of these least commandments, and shall teach men so to do, he shall in no wise be saved in the kingdom of heaven; but whosoever shall do and teach these commandments of the law until it be fulfilled, the same shall be called great, and shall be saved in the kingdom of heaven."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":4,"verse":1,"english":"And suffer us not to be led into temptation, but deliver us from evil."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":4,"verse":2,"english":"The light of the body is the eye; if therefore thine eye be single to the glory of God, thy whole body shall be full of light."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":4,"verse":3,"english":"And, again, I say unto you, Go ye into the world, and care not for the world; for the world will hate you, and will persecute you, and will turn you out of their synagogues."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":4,"verse":4,"english":"Nevertheless, ye shall go forth from house to house, teaching the people; and I will go before you."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":4,"verse":5,"english":"And your heavenly Father will provide for you, whatsoever things ye need for food, what ye shall eat; and for raiment, what ye shall wear or put on."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":5,"verse":1,"english":"Now these are the words which Jesus taught his disciples that they should say unto the people."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":5,"verse":2,"english":"Judge not unrighteously, that ye be not judged; but judge righteous judgment."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":5,"verse":3,"english":"And again, ye shall say unto them, Why is it that thou beholdest the mote that is in thy brother’s eye, but considerest not the beam that is in thine own eye?"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":5,"verse":4,"english":"Or how wilt thou say to thy brother, Let me pull out the mote out of thine eye; and canst not behold a beam in thine own eye?"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":5,"verse":5,"english":"And Jesus said unto his disciples, Beholdest thou the scribes, and the Pharisees, and the priests, and the Levites? They teach in their synagogues, but do not observe the law, nor the commandments; and all have gone out of the way, and are under sin."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":5,"verse":6,"english":"Go thou and say unto them, Why teach ye men the law and the commandments, when ye yourselves are the children of corruption?"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":5,"verse":7,"english":"Say unto them, Ye hypocrites, first cast out the beam out of thine own eye; and then shalt thou see clearly to cast out the mote out of thy brother’s eye."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":6,"verse":1,"english":"Then said the Pharisees unto him, Why will ye not receive us with our baptism, seeing we keep the whole law?"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":6,"verse":2,"english":"But Jesus said unto them, Ye keep not the law. If ye had kept the law, ye would have received me, for I am he who gave the law."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":6,"verse":3,"english":"I receive not you with your baptism, because it profiteth you nothing."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":6,"verse":4,"english":"For when that which is new is come, the old is ready to be put away."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":7,"verse":1,"english":"But the days will come, when the violent shall have no power; for all the prophets and the law prophesied that it should be thus until John."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":7,"verse":2,"english":"Yea, as many as have prophesied have foretold of these days."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":7,"verse":3,"english":"And if ye will receive it, verily, he was the Elias, who was for to come and prepare all things."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":8,"verse":1,"english":"Then came some of the scribes and said unto him, Master, it is written that, Every sin shall be forgiven; but ye say, Whosoever speaketh against the Holy Ghost shall not be forgiven. And they asked him, saying, How can these things be?"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":8,"verse":2,"english":"And he said unto them, When the unclean spirit is gone out of a man, he walketh through dry places, seeking rest and findeth none; but when a man speaketh against the Holy Ghost, then he saith, I will return into my house from whence I came out; and when he is come, he findeth him empty, swept and garnished; for the good spirit leaveth him unto himself."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":9,"verse":1,"english":"The harvest is the end of the world, or the destruction of the wicked."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":9,"verse":2,"english":"The reapers are the angels, or the messengers sent of heaven."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":9,"verse":3,"english":"As, therefore, the tares are gathered and burned in the fire, so shall it be in the end of this world, or the destruction of the wicked."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":9,"verse":4,"english":"For in that day, before the Son of man shall come, he shall send forth his angels and messengers of heaven."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":9,"verse":5,"english":"And they shall gather out of his kingdom all things that offend, and them which do iniquity, and shall cast them out among the wicked; and there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":9,"verse":6,"english":"For the world shall be burned with fire."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":10,"verse":1,"english":"Then said Jesus unto his disciples, If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross and follow me."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":10,"verse":2,"english":"And now for a man to take up his cross, is to deny himself all ungodliness, and every worldly lust, and keep my commandments."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":10,"verse":3,"english":"Break not my commandments for to save your lives; for whosoever will save his life in this world, shall lose it in the world to come."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":10,"verse":4,"english":"And whosoever will lose his life in this world, for my sake, shall find it in the world to come."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":10,"verse":5,"english":"Therefore, forsake the world, and save your souls; for what is a man profited, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul? Or what shall a man give in exchange for his soul?"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":11,"verse":1,"english":"And Jesus answered and said unto them, Elias truly shall first come, and restore all things, as the prophets have written."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":11,"verse":2,"english":"And again I say unto you that Elias has come already, concerning whom it is written, Behold, I will send my messenger, and he shall prepare the way before me; and they knew him not, and have done unto him, whatsoever they listed."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":11,"verse":3,"english":"Likewise shall also the Son of man suffer of them."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":11,"verse":4,"english":"But I say unto you, Who is Elias? Behold, this is Elias, whom I send to prepare the way before me."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":11,"verse":5,"english":"Then the disciples understood that he spake unto them of John the Baptist, and also of another who should come and restore all things, as it is written by the prophets."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":12,"verse":1,"english":"For the Son of man is come to save that which was lost, and to call sinners to repentance; but these little ones have no need of repentance, and I will save them."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":13,"verse":1,"english":"Then were there brought unto him little children, that he should put his hands on them and pray. And the disciples rebuked them, saying, There is no need, for Jesus hath said, Such shall be saved."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":14,"verse":1,"english":"For he that believed not John concerning me, cannot believe me, except he first repent."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":14,"verse":2,"english":"And when the chief priests and Pharisees had heard his parables, they perceived that he spake of them."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":14,"verse":3,"english":"And they said among themselves, Shall this man think that he alone can spoil this great kingdom? And they were angry with him."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":14,"verse":4,"english":"But when they sought to lay hands on him, they feared the multitude, because they learned that the multitude took him for a prophet."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":14,"verse":5,"english":"And now his disciples came to him, and Jesus said unto them, Marvel ye at the words of the parable which I spake unto them?"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":14,"verse":6,"english":"Verily, I say unto you, I am the stone, and those wicked ones reject me."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":14,"verse":7,"english":"I am the head of the corner. These Jews shall fall upon me, and shall be broken."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":15,"verse":1,"english":"And call no one your creator upon the earth, or your heavenly Father; for one is your creator and heavenly Father, even he who is in heaven."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":16,"verse":1,"english":"And as they were eating, Jesus took bread and brake it, and blessed it, and gave to his disciples, and said, Take, eat; this is in remembrance of my body which I give a ransom for you."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":16,"verse":2,"english":"For this is in remembrance of my blood of the new testament, which is shed for as many as shall believe on my name, for the remission of their sins."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":16,"verse":3,"english":"And I give unto you a commandment, that ye shall observe to do the things which ye have seen me do, and bear record of me even unto the end."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":17,"verse":1,"english":"Then Judas, who had betrayed him, when he saw that he was condemned, repented himself, and brought again the thirty pieces of silver to the chief priests and elders,"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":17,"verse":2,"english":"Saying, I have sinned in that I have betrayed the innocent blood."},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":17,"verse":3,"english":"And they said unto him, What is that to us? See thou to it; thy sins be upon thee."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"In that day thou shalt come, O Lord; and I will put my trust in thee. Thou shalt say unto thy people, for mine ear hath heard thy voice; thou shalt say unto every soul, Flee unto my mountain; and the righteous shall flee like a bird that is let go from the snare of the fowler."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"For the wicked bend their bow; lo, they make ready their arrow upon the string, that they may privily shoot at the upright in heart, to destroy their foundation."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":1,"verse":3,"english":"But the foundations of the wicked shall be destroyed, and what can they do?"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":1,"verse":4,"english":"For the Lord, when he shall come into his holy temple, sitting upon God’s throne in heaven, his eyes shall pierce the wicked."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":1,"verse":5,"english":"Behold his eyelids shall try the children of men, and he shall redeem the righteous, and they shall be tried. The Lord loveth the righteous, but the wicked, and him that loveth violence, his soul hateth."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"The fool hath said in his heart, There is no man that hath seen God. Because he showeth himself not unto us, therefore there is no God. Behold, they are corrupt; they have done abominable works, and none of them doeth good."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"For the Lord looked down from heaven upon the children of men, and by his voice said unto his servant, Seek ye among the children of men, to see if there are any that do understand God. And he opened his mouth unto the Lord, and said, Behold, all these who say they are thine."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":2,"verse":3,"english":"The Lord answered, and said, They are all gone aside, they are together become filthy, thou canst behold none of them that are doing good, no, not one."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":2,"verse":4,"english":"All they have for their teachers are workers of iniquity, and there is no knowledge in them. They are they who eat up my people. They eat bread and call not upon the Lord."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":2,"verse":5,"english":"They are in great fear, for God dwells in the generation of the righteous. He is the counsel of the poor, because they are ashamed of the wicked, and flee unto the Lord, for their refuge."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":2,"verse":6,"english":"They are ashamed of the counsel of the poor because the Lord is his refuge."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":2,"verse":7,"english":"Oh that Zion were established out of heaven, the salvation of Israel. O Lord, when wilt thou establish Zion? When the Lord bringeth back the captivity of his people, Jacob shall rejoice, Israel shall be glad."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"Lift up your heads, O ye generations of Jacob; and be ye lifted up; and the Lord strong and mighty; the Lord mighty in battle, who is the king of glory, shall establish you forever."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":3,"verse":2,"english":"And he will roll away the heavens; and will come down to redeem his people; to make you an everlasting name; to establish you upon his everlasting rock."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":3,"verse":3,"english":"Lift up your heads, O ye generations of Jacob; lift up your heads, ye everlasting generations, and the Lord of hosts, the king of kings;"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":3,"verse":4,"english":"Even the king of glory shall come unto you; and shall redeem his people, and shall establish them in righteousness. Selah."},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":4,"verse":1,"english":"And, notwithstanding my love, they are my adversaries; yet I will continue in prayer for them."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"The Revelation of John, a servant of God, which was given unto him of Jesus Christ, to show unto his servants things which must shortly come to pass, that he sent and signified by his angel unto his servant John,"},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"Who bore record of the word of God, and of the testimony of Jesus Christ, and of all things that he saw."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":1,"verse":3,"english":"Blessed are they who read, and they who hear and understand the words of this prophecy, and keep those things which are written therein, for the time of the coming of the Lord draweth nigh."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":1,"verse":4,"english":"Now this is the testimony of John to the seven servants who are over the seven churches in Asia. Grace unto you, and peace from him who is, and who was, and who is to come; who hath sent forth his angel from before his throne, to testify unto those who are the seven servants over the seven churches."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"Behold, I will cast her into hell, and them that commit adultery with her into great tribulation, except they repent of their deeds."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"And to him who overcometh, and keepeth my commandments unto the end, will I give power over many kingdoms;"},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":2,"verse":3,"english":"And he shall rule them with the word of God; and they shall be in his hands as the vessels of clay in the hands of a potter; and he shall govern them by faith, with equity and justice, even as I received of my Father."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"And I beheld, and, lo, in the midst of the throne and of the four beasts, and in the midst of the elders, stood a Lamb as it had been slain, having twelve horns and twelve eyes, which are the twelve servants of God, sent forth into all the earth."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":4,"verse":1,"english":"And there appeared a great sign in heaven, in the likeness of things on the earth; a woman clothed with the sun, and the moon under her feet, and upon her head a crown of twelve stars."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":4,"verse":2,"english":"And the woman being with child, cried, travailing in birth, and pained to be delivered."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":4,"verse":3,"english":"And she brought forth a man child, who was to rule all nations with a rod of iron; and her child was caught up unto God and his throne."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":4,"verse":4,"english":"And there appeared another sign in heaven; and behold, a great red dragon, having seven heads and ten horns, and seven crowns upon his heads. And his tail drew the third part of the stars of heaven, and did cast them to the earth. And the dragon stood before the woman which was delivered, ready to devour her child after it was born."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":5,"verse":1,"english":"And out of his mouth proceedeth the word of God, and with it he will smite the nations; and he will rule them with the word of his mouth; and he treadeth the winepress in the fierceness and wrath of Almighty God."},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":5,"verse":2,"english":"And the remnant were slain with the word of him that sat upon the horse, which word proceeded out of his mouth; and all the fowls were filled with their flesh."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":1,"verse":1,"english":"But if we remain in our unrighteousness and commend the righteousness of God, how dare we say, God is unrighteous who taketh vengeance? (I speak as a man who fears God,)"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":1,"verse":2,"english":"God forbid; for then how shall God judge the world?"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":1,"verse":3,"english":"For if the truth of God hath more abounded through my lie, (as it is called of the Jews,) unto his glory; why yet am I also judged as a sinner? and not received? Because we are slanderously reported;"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":1,"verse":4,"english":"And some affirm that we say, (whose damnation is just,) Let us do evil that good may come. But this is false."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":2,"verse":1,"english":"For if Abraham were justified by the law of works, he hath to glory in himself; but not of God."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":2,"verse":2,"english":"For what saith the scripture? Abraham believed God, and it was counted unto him for righteousness."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":2,"verse":3,"english":"Now to him who is justified by the law of works, is the reward reckoned, not of grace, but of debt."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":2,"verse":4,"english":"But to him that seeketh not to be justified by the law of works, but believeth on him who justifieth not the ungodly, his faith is counted for righteousness."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":3,"verse":1,"english":"For when we were in the flesh, the motions of sin, which were not according to the law, did work in our members to bring forth fruit unto death."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":3,"verse":2,"english":"But now we are delivered from the law wherein we were held, being dead to the law, that we should serve in newness of spirit, and not in the oldness of the letter."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":3,"verse":3,"english":"What shall we say then? Is the law sin? God forbid. Nay, I had not known sin, but by the law; for I had not known lust, except the law had said, Thou shalt not covet."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":3,"verse":4,"english":"For once I was alive without transgression of the law, but when the commandment of Christ came, sin revived, and I died."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":3,"verse":5,"english":"And now I see another law, even the commandment of Christ, and it is imprinted in my mind."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":3,"verse":6,"english":"But my members are warring against the law of my mind, and bringing me into captivity to the law of sin which is in my members."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":4,"verse":1,"english":"So then they that are after the flesh cannot please God."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":5,"verse":1,"english":"For, for this cause pay ye your consecrations also unto them; for they are God’s ministers, attending continually upon this very thing."},{"book":"Romans","chapter":5,"verse":2,"english":"But first, render to all their dues, according to custom, tribute to whom tribute, custom to whom custom, that your consecrations may be done in fear of him to whom fear belongs, and in honor of him to whom honor belongs."}];
